/*
# CMS 4/4 — Phase 3 content import (seed)

GENERATED from the site's current hardcoded content (the data files in src/lib and the
inline constants in src/pages / src/components) on 2026-09-26.
The JSON mirrors what the site renders today, value for value.

Requires migrations 1/3, 2/3 and 3/3 to be applied first (checked below).

WHAT IT WRITES (only INSERTs into new/empty tables, never UPDATEs or DELETEs
existing rows):
--   global               1
--   page                 5
--   form                 13
--   immigration_service  10
--   visa_destination     8
--   travel_package       12
--   travel_destination   5
--   news_article         7
--   testimonial          copied from the live `testimonials` table
--                        (or the 3 hardcoded fallbacks if it has none)
--   media rows           108 (one per image URL, marked pending-import)
--   form_field_mappings  13 (CRM routing, one per form)
Then publishes every document that has never been published.

READS (does not modify): testimonials, pages/sections/content_blocks
(the live testimonials heading).

ATOMIC: runs as one transaction (db push wraps each migration; the SQL Editor
runs a multi-statement script atomically).

SAFE TO RE-RUN: every insert is ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING / WHERE NOT EXISTS and
only never-published documents are published, so editor changes made after
the first run are never overwritten.

VISIBLE EFFECT ON THE LIVE SITE: none. The website does not read these tables
until Phase 4.
BEHAVIOUR CHANGE: once form_field_mappings has rows, every NEW form submission
automatically creates a CRM lead (contacts row). Existing submissions are untouched.
*/


do $$
begin
  if to_regclass('public.cms_documents') is null
     or to_regclass('public.cms_published') is null
     or not exists (select 1 from information_schema.columns
                    where table_schema = 'public' and table_name = 'media' and column_name = 'source_url') then
    raise exception 'Apply CMS migrations 20260926120000, 20260926120100 and 20260926120200 first';
  end if;
end;
$$;

